ased writer's declared ids match their re-derivation from the construction registry (VAL-002)"},"readers":{"v1.0":{"description":"the shipped schemas/v1 family, digest-pinned at generation time","stems":{"ingest-envelope":{"sha256":"78ce1e0c8c5545d8e2366b5b06295059a9c877eebdb61107648a580f58ccab77","source":"schemas/v1/ingest-envelope.json"},"ingest-receipt":{"sha256":"29e5206e4efd78c1e775e8766f76ce65710051bb5bf316a70effd9f39b5f69f2","source":"schemas/v1/ingest-receipt.json"},"ingest-request":{"sha256":"5bfbf6741c8492f843fa344667ce219464748b9fb53af2add5aa0db3a1d73da6","source":"schemas/v1/ingest-request.json"},"occurrence-manifest":{"sha256":"3f24ae54de2a1318d04056d2b4d6c8c547310b87ce0ef1f2c1300322f9b23629","source":"schemas/v1/occurrence-manifest.json"},"upload-attestation":{"sha256":"49d4566e0b2166577bd39f4ce3409cbbc5efd8487adabefe1203ad24453dca86","source":"schemas/v1/upload-attestation.json"}}},"v1.1":{"description":"the same family plus exactly one pinned additive optional field on each retain-ignore durable record; every other stem is shared with v1.0 unchanged","projected":{"ingest-envelope":{"additive_fields":["client_build"],"file":"readers/v1.1/ingest-envelope.json"},"ingest-receipt":{"additive_fields":["server_build"],"file":"readers/v1.1/ingest-receipt.json"},"occurrence-manifest":{"additive_fields":["adapter_build_id"],"file":"readers/v1.1/occurrence-manifest.json"},"upload-attestation":{"additive_fields":["uploader_agent_version"],"file":"readers/v1.1/upload-attestation.json"}},"shared":["ingest-request"]}},"rules":{"adapter-projection-preserved":"adapter projection: the adapter + projection version is preserved in provenance and is an identity input, so a bump mints new occurrences instead of overwriting","additive-optional-within-major":"within a v1 schema, new optional fields are additive","derived-pipeline-isolated":"derived pipeline: name + version; rebuildable, versioned keys under a derived prefix that never overwrites raw data","no-floats":"protocol structures contain no floating-point values","readers-retain-old-versions":"occurrence and attestation axes: readers retain old-version support (a newer reader still accepts the older writer's documents)","requires-new-major":"new required fields, redefined fields, changed identity rules, or grown fail-closed enums require a new major","route-major":"HTTP route /v1/ingest: breaking wire changes use a new route major (a version=2 envelope media type is rejected at framing; an unknown protocol_version fails closed)","security-enums-fail-closed":"unknown security- or identity-bearing enum values fail closed","storage-layout-prefix-stable":"storage layout: a v1 key prefix is never silently repurposed; a new encoder is a new named profile and key segment","unknown-major-fails-closed":"envelope/occurrence/attestation/receipt majors: an unknown major on any axis fails closed","unknown-optional-retained-in-signed-bytes":"old readers ignore the semantics of unknown optional data while retaining it inside signed bytes"},"scan_version":1,"scenarios":[{"asserts":["the v1.0 reader accepts the v1.1 writer's envelope: the unknown optional member passes the open retain-ignore shape","the member survives a parse -> canonicalize round trip byte-identically and the canonical envelope bytes (the material the ingest-attempt-v1 envelope_digest covers) are pinned including it","every identity and object key equals the baseline's: the old reader ignores the member's semantics (VAL-002 re-derivation still matches the declared occurrence_id)"],"framing":{"outcome":"accepted_at_framing","part_one_media_type":"application/vnd.agent-archivist.envelope+json;version=1","route":"/v1/ingest"},"id":"orn-additive-envelope","identity":{"artifact_hash":"0438d5c38d1b36b289ecc4f0fcb707e3661408b8973b6d50764a2cf2b163ac7a","attestation_id":"95fa374c2e4113ddc39e5548d26b06757dcf5ca7e40ab0dbc632a847e6b90f1f","blob_digest":"e1ef89ecbbdd273d0d7ddc471e0c4c6b2ef3de193c1e3cfef970cd75eb2f7629","occurrence_id":"